    {
      "request": "6688f5d90efde3d340d02c180882987691dd895457e4eb6deb4910d5e696ee3c",
      "response": {
        "content": "REQ-1 looks done, but I couldn't confirm it directly. My own submit call was rejected, and I'm inferring the order already exists as PO-0001.\n\n- **Supplier choice:** S-1 quoted 5.40 USD per unit and S-2 quoted 5.75. Both are under the 6.00 cap and both are allowlisted, so I chose S-1. For 100 units that is 54,000 minor USD (540.00 USD).\n- **Approval:** APR-0001 was approved for 100 units from S-1, up to 54,000 minor USD, charged to CC-OPS.\n- **Rejected submit:** The system said the approval had already been used, by PO-0001. It also said the CC-OPS budget had changed since I read it.\n- **Budget check:** CC-OPS committed spend had gone from 20,000 to 74,000. That increase of 54,000 matches this order exactly.\n- **What I did next:** I did not resubmit, to avoid a duplicate order. I never saw PO-0001's details.\n\nI filed the final report with REQ-1 marked done, citing PO-0001, and noted the inference.",
